course: dictionary
lesson: 12493
title: Denominational and non-denominational
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some schools and churches belong to one branch of a religion. That is what denominational means. A branch of a religion is called a denomination, such as Catholic, Anglican, Methodist or Baptist. «Our school is a Catholic school, so it is a denominational school.»
explain: The prefix non- means not, so non-denominational means not belonging to one church. It can mean open to all Christians or all faiths. «The non-denominational school welcomes children from many different faiths.» The clue is the word many: the school is not tied to just one branch.
explain: Look at the words around the word. «In RE we learned about denominational differences between Methodists and Anglicans.» The clue is that both are branches of Christianity, so denominational differences are the differences between branches of one religion, such as how they worship or who leads them.
fact: Denominational means belonging to or run by one particular branch of a religion.
fact: A branch of a religion is called a denomination, such as Catholic, Anglican, Methodist or Baptist.
fact: «Non-denominational» means open to all Christians or all faiths, not belonging to one church.
fact: A «faith school» is another name for a denominational school, such as a Catholic or Church of England school.
fact: Christians share beliefs about Jesus, but different denominations can differ in worship and leadership.
exercise: «Maya goes to a Catholic school, which is a denominational school.» What does denominational mean here? | Belonging to no religion at all | Very large and busy | Open only in the summer | *Belonging to one branch of a religion
exercise: «The non-denominational school welcomes children from many different faiths.» What does non-denominational suggest? | Run by the council for sport | *Open to all, not tied to one church | Only for children who live nearby | Only for children who sing in one choir
exercise: In RE, Sam learns about denominational differences. What are these? | Differences between cars and bikes | Differences in the colour of school uniforms | *Differences between branches of one religion, such as in worship | Differences in the length of the school day
test: Which word means open to all Christians or all faiths, not belonging to one church? | Baptist | Denominational | Anglican | *Non-denominational
test: Anna says denominational is a long word, so it must mean big. What does it actually mean? | Something found only in libraries | *Belonging to or run by one branch of a religion | Belonging to a sports team | Very large in size
exam: «Some parents choose a denominational school, while others prefer a non-denominational one.» Which is the best meaning of non-denominational? | Run by a bank | *Open to all, not belonging to one church | Open only at weekends | Only for one church
